WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.740
Hi, everyone, Kaleido Star is about to start.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.480
When you watch Kaleido Star,
please keep your room brightly lit,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.880
and sit as far from the TV as you can, okay?

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.550
Well, well, well.
Doesn't it make you really anxious

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.040
when you go somewhere you don't know?

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.150
Everything I bump into
is something new for me.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.980
Applying something I've already learned
or memorized is not good enough.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.580
I know it happens all the time, but

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.990
I wonder why they still keep getting
mad at me?! I wonder. I wonder!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be someplace</i>

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:35.740
<i>Dare mo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.240
<i>It has to be somewhere</i>

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.240
<i>Dokoka ni aru</i>

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:45.940
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:45.940
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja nai</i>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:01:00.300
<i>Remember how I used to say
I could make it to the end?</i>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:01:00.300
<i>Saigo made yareru to ittetane</i>

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.670
<i>I must have been pretending to be tough</i>

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:06.670
<i>Kitto tsuyogatte itanda</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:15.380
<i>Everything I did was reckless
and it never got me anywhere</i>

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:15.380
<i>Itsudatte muchabakka de
zutto karamawari de</i>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>But you alone were always beside me</i>

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>Dakedo anata dake ga soba ni ita</i>

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.620
<i>The dream everyone is looking for
must be somewhere</i>

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.620
<i>Daremo sagashiteru yume wa kitto aru</i>

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.230
<i>You can start going forward</i>

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.230
<i>Aruki daseru</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.770
<i>From this moment, something will start</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.770
<i>Koko kara nani kaga hajimaru</i>

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>I want to believe that</i>

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>Shinjite itai</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:46.310
<i>The light I haven't seen yet
is beaming toward the promised place</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:46.310
<i>Mada minu hikari yakusoku no
basho e to tsuzuite yuku</i>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:56.780
<i>Until your dream comes true someday,
you're not alone</i>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:56.780
<i>Negai ga itsuka kanau made hitori ja naisa</i>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.930
Great work!

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.340
We're off starting tomorrow.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.410
Since we have a week, we can really relax.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.050
Once in a while, it would be nice
if we could travel or something.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.210
You're full of energy, Sora.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.290
I'm going to take a break and relax.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.420
Me too.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.660
Really?

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.530
I feel like visiting a town
I've never visited before.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.620
You know, just let loose!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.730
Sora.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.590
What?

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.220
This...

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.600
What? This is an airline ticket.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.810
Could you possibly be rewarding me,
for my hard work,

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.210
with a trip somewhere?

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.580
Possibly? Possibly?

00:02:58.750 --> 00:02:59.680
Congratulations.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.910
Your dream came true.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:01.910
It's work.

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.720
Well...

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.380
For now, at least your dream came true...

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.130
I want you to make a guest appearance

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:10.360
Work, work, work... I have to work...

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:10.360
I want you to make a guest appearance

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.730
Work, work, work... I have to work...

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.730
in my old friend Mr. Pack's circus.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:24.910
An ordeal...

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.910
The card signifies sacrifice.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.000
It's ominous.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.720
Mysterious Amazing Circus

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.720
"Mysterious Amazing Circus"

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.550
Mysterious Amazing Circus

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.520
Over there, I will be your manager.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.530
So, please expect me to act accordingly.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.720
Yes.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.890
But, I'm glad you're coming with me.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.460
I guess life is good sometimes.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.030
We're going to a place called
Theatrical Camp.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.370
Theatrical Camp?

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.180
It's a mobile circus.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.680
Their highlights are,

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.370
fire-breathing, knife throwing,
whip tricks, and keg juggling.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:07.980
I see...

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.880
I wonder if I also need to do Fire-Breathing.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.280
I doubt it.

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.880
Strangers!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.630
Ken.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.470
Oh... Don't worry.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.430
It's supposed to be around here.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.400
Oh, that way!

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.270
I have been waiting for you,
Miss Sora Naegino.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.300
Welcome to Theatrical Camp.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.170
She really is breathing flame.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.600
Here it goes!

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.050
Sorry.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.230
Amazing...

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.820
Even the audience is participating.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.500
Hey, Milo!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:37.510
I know nothing.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.640
You ate it!

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.580
That's enough, Tank!

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.380
Leave the place quick
once you finish your juggling!

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.080
But it makes the kids happy...

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.110
Don't come up with an excuse!

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:48.580
Okay, okay.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.480
Excuse me...

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:49.880
Don't make me repeat
the same thing over and over!

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:50.790
Wait!

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:50.790
Don't make me repeat
the same thing over and over!

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.020
I didn't eat it!

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.050
Then who ate it?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.450
I don't know.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.620
EXCUSE ME!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.160
I'm introducing a guest to you.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.360
This is Miss Sora Naegino.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.400
I came from Kaleido Stage!

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.040
It's nice to meet you.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.840
I'm Sora's manager, Ken Robbins.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.720
Kaleido Stage...

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:26.980
Here!

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.920
This evening's beef stew has the best meat.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.890
Meat, meat!

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.700
For tomorrow's show, since we have a guest,

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.900
why don't we do the one
we haven't done in a while?

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.300
Miss Sora Naegino...

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.530
I want you to play the leading
part, the Princess.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.200
The leading part?

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:45.470
Yes.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.570
And it's the role of a princess?

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:49.840
I don't know if I'm capable of
playing that role.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:51.800
Maybe it's impossible...

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.310
What?

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.910
Impossible, impossible, impossible...

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.620
Well... I will do my best.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.680
Impossible, impossible, impossible...

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.550
The story itself is very simple.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.330
The role we want you to play

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:10.370
is a heroine who rescues
her younger twin sisters,

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.390
who are taken by a witch.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.000
All right.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.100
Mila and Milo are throwing away
carrots again, Dominique.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.970
If you do it again, you'll have no dinner!

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.440
Yes...

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.740
Pamela, you're going to play
the villain, a witch.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:29.820
Yes.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.010
Tank, you're going to play a glutton
with supernatural strength.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:32.980
All right.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:34.760
And...

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.590
You will fight against a
knife throwing monster man.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.260
And then you will head for the witch's nest.

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:41.830
Pack, don't forget about me.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.230
Of course, Mr. Dio.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.160
He is the heroine's only ally.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:50.170
Both of them cooperate
and rescue the twins,

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:50.810
and they fall in love and...

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:51.670
Lov-

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:51.670
and they fall in love and...

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.710
It comes to a happy ending.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:54.680
It's nice to meet you.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.840
It's nice to meet you too.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.750
I don't think they need to fall in love.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.240
Okay, okay.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.860
Can you feed him milk?

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:09.820
All right.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:10.830
Chocolate.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.130
Tiger.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.220
A lion handler.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.630
Dog.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.000
This script talks about the story,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.460
Stuffed animals.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.460
This script talks about the story,

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.730
This script talks about the story,

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.570
but it doesn't say anything
about how we perform.

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.770
I wonder what I'm supposed to do.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:20.970
Lake!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:20.970
I wonder what I'm supposed to do.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:21.630
Lake!

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:22.170
Well, never mind.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:22.730
We already said that one.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:22.730
Well, never mind.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.270
We already said that one.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.270
I'll ask during rehearsal tomorrow.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:24.840
No, we didn't!

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.540
No, we didn't!

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.540
I think I should rest well today.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:26.740
No, we didn't!

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.610
It already came up!

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.980
No, it did NOT!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:29.910
Yes, it did!

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:29.910
No, it did NOT!

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:30.750
You're annoying!

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.810
It came up, it came up,
it came up, it came up!

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:35.080
It came up, it came up, it came up!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.820
I can't sleep...

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:48.130
Ken...

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.530
Sora,

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:51.790
the stars are beautiful.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:53.930
Yes, they are.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.070
Ken...

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:56.870
What?

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.010
Thank you for everything.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.370
Huh? What? All of a sudden...

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.610
Because you always help me
whenever I'm in trouble.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:07.340
And you encourage me.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.820
Without your help,

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.390
I doubt I would've had the chance
to play the Little Mermaid.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.320
Or the chance to co-star
with Miss Layla, either.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:15.260
I don't think it's true.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.790
You got them because you worked hard.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:19.360
I wonder.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.360
No, really.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.520
You're a hard worker.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.630
You work too hard.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:26.960
I sometimes feel that you may
end up out of my league.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.170
Huh?

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.570
Oh... It's nothing.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:33.000
I think you should get some sleep tonight.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.180
Well... It's noisy and...

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.580
Oh... Really?

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:38.880
But, I will do my best and try to sleep.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.600
I think that would be better.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.480
Okay, I will do my best and sleep!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.530
That baby cried all night long.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.690
Yeah. Tank's snoring was pretty bad too.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.270
Nobody's here.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.810
The male cast isn't here either.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:09.780
What? Then what about the rehearsal?

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.200
They're probably not going to have one.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.550
What? They're not?

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.780
Well...

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.650
They almost never rehearse.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.120
What?!

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.090
Then what's everyone doing now?

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.190
Who knows?

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.020
Until the evening performance,
it's their free time.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:27.390
What?

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:29.520
That's coming from the stage.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.190
Mr. Dio!

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:34.440
I'm glad.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.430
I was wondering what to do
since nobody was here.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.000
I bet everyone went out to have some fun.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:43.040
People in town give us a warm reception,

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.640
and we get free food and drink.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.780
Oh, wait a moment!

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:49.350
You really don't rehearse at all?

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:51.080
I can't perform without a rehearsal.

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:52.940
Well... What shall I do?

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.850
Well then, I will teach you
one important thing.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:56.890
Yes.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.800
Since you saw the show yesterday,
I think you already know this,

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.700
but each member has something
that they're good at.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:08.190
The story itself is there just so
each of us can show off our forte.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.710
So always pay attention to the
audience's reaction, and proceed.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.470
Proceed while paying attention
to the audience's reaction...

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:17.710
That's right.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.610
What you want to show the audience
is all up to you.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:21.880
Relax.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.910
Thank you very much.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.950
It's up to me...

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.800
Pamela!

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:47.910
You're great!

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.010
Princess!

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.340
If you wish to rescue your sisters,

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.440
you should come to my castle!

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.340
Help!

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:04.690
I wonder, can I show up already?
I wonder... I wonder...

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.260
What shall I do?!

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:08.660
Hurry and get out!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.270
I'm a heroine.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.460
So I have to act like one.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.810
Mila, Milo where did you go?

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:18.670
I hope the witch didn't...

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:24.380
Oh, wait!

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:26.870
I still haven't finished my lines yet...

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.050
Sora...

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:34.610
It looks like everything is going smoothly.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.650
Going smoothly?

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:42.630
She's terrible.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:02.040
Wait! Excuse me!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.840
Oh! Beer kegs!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.290
Now is indeed the time
to test the Princess's courage!

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:21.130
Please... Please...

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.400
Please don't move.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.480
I'm here, Princess!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.410
I can't finish the show like this.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.760
Not like this!

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.640
What?

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:08.170
You're nothing!

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.800
What are you people thinking?

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.470
If this is how she's going to be treated,

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:32.340
I'll refuse to let her
appear on stage tomorrow.

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.110
If Miss Sora Naegino insists on that,

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.410
there's nothing I can do.

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:44.970
It seems showing a new member in trouble
is all part of the show.

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:46.790
If you want to leave,

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:49.090
I can explain the situation to Kalos.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.230
I don't mind them
making fun of my mistakes.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:54.000
But, it's not like that.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.400
They were all laughing at me
because I was a stranger.

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.800
Yesterday's show...

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.870
I thought it was amazing.
The audience and cast became one.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.910
It was so exciting.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.600
But, today, from the beginning to the end,

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.940
They treated me like a stranger.

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:11.240
They didn't even allow me to perform.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.740
Are you talking about Pamela?

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:14.780
Mr. Dio!

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.220
It's terrible what Pamela did to you.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.450
But did you notice Pamela
before you grabbed the swing?

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:22.820
What?

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:26.120
You stole Pamela's thunder.

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:27.290
Oh...

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.490
So that's why...

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.800
I...

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:33.820
Thank you, Mr. Dio.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:39.200
Go to sleep already!

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:47.950
What?

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.340
I'm sorry for what I did to you back then.

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.990
I bet you feel like going back already.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:57.090
It's not so easy that you'll get applause

00:15:57.090 --> 00:16:00.960
just for following the script
like you do at Kaleido Stage.

00:16:01.030 --> 00:16:03.520
Kaleido Stage isn't that easy either!

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.640
I'm not leaving yet.

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.040
Really...

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.640
While I perform at this place,

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.970
I will appear on stage
as one of members here.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.700
So, tomorrow, please make sure to catch me.

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:20.580
If I feel like it.

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:33.930
Is this a foolish person's upright position?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.720
Fool!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:34.720
Is this a foolish person's upright position?

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.930
Just as I feared.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:40.030
You look upset after you were
tossed about in the storms of life.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.300
Did you come because
you were worried about me?

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:43.540
That's right.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.170
I endured staying inside that tight suit case.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:47.070
Still,

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.780
I never expected you to get so upset.

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:50.300
I'm glad I'm here.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.810
Thank you, Fool.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.310
I'm glad I'm here, too!

00:16:56.020 --> 00:16:57.480
NO!

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:02.950
Oh... A roach...

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:06.890
First,

00:17:06.890 --> 00:17:09.730
Let's start with learning more
about the stage.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:10.860
Okay.

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:13.700
As I expected, the stage as a whole is small.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.830
It means there's not much distance
between you and the audience.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.310
To tell you the truth, at Kaleido Stage,

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.900
the audience can't see
the performers' subtle expressions.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:24.740
But here, the audience can see your
expressions even when you're in trouble.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:25.900
Okay.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:30.620
Doing the same show I do at Kaleido Stage
doesn't attract the audience here.

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:37.180
I have to perform while observing
the cast members and the audience.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:40.960
Unless I can do that, I can't be one of them.

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:44.000
Princess!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.330
If you wish to rescue your sisters,

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:47.420
you should come to my castle!

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.900
Help!

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.140
Okay!

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:55.110
Yes!

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.810
Mila, Milo, where did you go?

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:06.550
Were they kidnapped by the witch?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:10.090
I will make sure to rescue them.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.180
I will!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:13.730
What?

00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:15.730
Did I miss something?

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:16.820
Oh...

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.100
Well, then...

00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:25.530
How about this?

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:30.170
Oh, here I go!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.780
Here, here, here, here!

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.280
Oh, beer kegs!

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.190
Thank you, thank you!

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:44.420
Princess, you're the best!

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.260
Sora Naegino!

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.590
Bravo!

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:47.590
Sora Naegino!

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:50.250
Good, I think I can do this.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:54.330
Ready!

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:57.260
Are you saying to hit the bull's-eye
right in that circle?

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.230
Yeah!

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.240
Not bad...

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.750
I'm here, Princess!

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:16.520
I will show you the leading role's maneuver.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:17.720
What?

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.040
What! Straight up?

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:39.640
Amazing.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.320
You're amazing, Miss Pamela!

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:17.180
I've never seen anything like that before!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.410
I can manage that maneuver
only one time in five.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.720
But, I didn't want to be outdone by you, so...

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.320
There is no way I can...

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:28.860
A great maneuver which may hurt you
isn't required here.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:30.930
The thing which is required here

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.800
is the ability to appear on stage everyday.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:36.540
Kaleido Stage isn't everything.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:41.370
I understood very well that each troupe
has a show it's best suited for.

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:45.540
I used to be in Kaleido Stage.

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:46.650
What?

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:49.520
But it wasn't my kind of place, you know...

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:51.250
I wasn't allowed to do what I wanted.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:54.020
Oh... Really?

00:20:54.090 --> 00:20:56.120
You seems like the kind who does
whatever you want to do.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:56.960
Well...

00:20:56.960 --> 00:20:59.950
I have no intention to act that way, but...

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:04.700
I bet you're just what
Kaleido Stage needs right now.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:09.030
Sadly though, it's the time to say goodbye.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.400
What?

00:21:10.400 --> 00:21:14.070
It seems Milo's twisted an ankle
during today's performance.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.310
It's earlier than the date we had in mind,

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:19.580
but we decided to cut the performance short.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:22.380
What are these?

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.880
Olives.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.890
Mr. Pack plants olives like these
at each place we camp.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.950
It's his hobby.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.290
They say that the olive,
the symbol of peace,

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:35.230
can sprout the next season even if
the place where it was burns down.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:38.170
I wish to be as strong as this olive.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.330
And, more importantly,

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.530
the olive is a must-have for a good salad.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:47.400
She is charming.

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:53.750
That princess role was played
by many people, including Pamela,

00:21:53.750 --> 00:21:56.150
but I thought she had such invaluable talent.

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:59.450
Unless someone nurtures her,

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.940
the flower of her talents will never bloom.

00:22:01.990 --> 00:22:02.960
I understand.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:06.790
I will make sure to nurture her talents.

00:22:07.690 --> 00:22:11.070
Pamela, please come to see our show too.

00:22:11.070 --> 00:22:12.370
If I feel like it.

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:14.270
What? That's not nice.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:22.340
Next Kaleido Star

00:22:23.080 --> 00:22:24.910
I'm afraid he no longer needs me.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:26.150
And so...

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:28.550
What? Miss Sarah was approached
by another company?

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:32.780
Not only that... It's a man and a woman's
ten year love!

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:35.560
An entangled love triangle...
I don't understand the complicated stuff.

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:39.080
But we can't just let things go
like this, right? Right? Right?

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:42.960
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"The Diva's Amazing Love"

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:43.130
The Diva's Amazing Love

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:43.130
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"The Diva's Amazing Love"

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:43.760
The Diva's Amazing Love

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.900
The Diva's Amazing Love

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.900
My wings are my dream and
on towards the sky...

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:48.090
The Diva's Amazing Love

00:22:51.440 --> 00:23:04.280
<i>I'm here between the sky and the roads,
and facing against the wind</i>

00:22:51.440 --> 00:23:04.280
<i>Boku wa koko ni iru
sora to michi no aida de mukai kaze</i>

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:18.170
<i>And I'm facing forward so the sorrow
doesn't rain down ever again</i>

00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:18.170
<i>Soshite mae o muiteiru
Mou nido to kanashimi ga furanai youni to</i>

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:24.100
<i>I came all the way here after
I jumped over that wall</i>

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:24.100
<i>Ano kabe o koete kokomade kitanda</i>

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:31.380
<i>There are many times
when I just want to run away</i>

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:31.380
<i>Nigedashitaku naru koto wa nando mo aru</i>

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:36.780
<i>But I'm still here,
so, I'm not daunted that much</i>

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:36.780
<i>Dakedo kokoni irunara taishite bibitte inai</i>

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:44.190
<i>The poem I scribbled down, I can just
start writing over from the beginning</i>

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:44.190
<i>Kakinaguri no uta "hajimekara yareba iisa"</i>

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:50.460
<i>Unable to write it well, I'm laughing</i>

00:23:44.190 --> 00:23:50.460
<i>Umaku kakenaku te boku wa waratte iru</i>
